# Deploy and server ops

## Pipeline (UU / Sound Strategy style)

```bash
./scripts/server-setup.sh          # one-time dirs + Apache templates
./scripts/server-db.sh dev|prod    # apt Postgres role/DB on :5432
./scripts/deploy.sh dev|prod       # build, rsync, venv, migrate, systemd, verify
```

`deploy.sh` forces target-canonical ports (dev 3010/8010, prod 3009/8009) even if `env.*.sh` has the wrong `PORT`/`API_PORT`.

## Env files

- `deploy/env.example.sh` → `deploy/env.dev.sh` / `deploy/env.prod.sh`
- Rendered to `<docroot>/app/.env` (Next) and `<docroot>/api/.env` (FastAPI)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` baked at **build** time — fix URLs before `deploy.sh`
- `DATABASE_URL` must use `127.0.0.1:5432` (never Docker ports 5439/5440)
- Prefer separate DBs: `rideconnect` (dev) vs `rideconnect_prod` (prod)

## Prod cutover

- Legacy WP vhost files in `sites-enabled` must be **removed** (not only `a2dissite`) — they are often plain files, not symlinks
- WP tree already under `/var/www/_backups/phantomequestrian.com/`
- Cert SANs already include apex, www, dev, api, api.dev

## Shell anti-patterns

| Pitfall | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| bash `source` of `.env` | Secrets with `#`/`^` break; let pydantic/alembic load `.env` from cwd |
| Incomplete `.venv` (dir exists, no pip) | Recreate when `python -m pip` fails |
| Verify wrong ports | Always use target defaults, not env `PORT` from the other target |
| `grep -c \|\| echo 0` | Use `grep -q` + explicit 0/1 flags |

## Services

| Target | systemd units |
|--------|----------------|
| dev | `rideconnect-web-dev`, `rideconnect-api-dev` |
| prod | `rideconnect-web`, `rideconnect-api` |

Debug: `journalctl -u rideconnect-api -n 40` / `curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8009/health`
